{
  "about": "Gate D.3 poll result vectors (V3.2 execution plan §4, D-47, owner ruling in Issue #9). Results come from per-block answer counts and eligible households per block. Defaults: at least 3 answers and 5 households for any grouping; the breakdown of a grouping is shown only if every option count is 0 or at least 3 and so is every option's complement, otherwise the whole breakdown is withheld (turnout only, options: null). A block is shown only if the whole audience's breakdown is, its own is safe, and the audience minus every set of shown blocks is safe too. 'options' maps option id to count; 'blocks' maps block code to its total. Issue #10: blocks are chosen without subset enumeration. Every shown block and the undisclosed remainder (all hidden blocks together) must be safe; the remainder may also be empty (no household, no answer), but never a group with households and fewer than 3 answers (that would show they stayed silent). While the remainder is not safe, the shown block that leaves it the fewest small figures goes back into it (at most 2k + 2 steps for k options). 'generate' describes many blocks compactly: 'count' blocks named prefix001, prefix002, … each with the same answers and households, or one named block. 'blocksShown' is the number of blocks shown; 'hidden' lists blocks that must not be shown; 'maxMs' bounds the time of one call. Block households must add up to the audience exactly.",
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "opt_1",
      "label": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "id": "opt_2",
      "label": "No"
    }
  ],
